        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0652" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg582"/>

                <head>No. 354.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Langston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 17,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 201.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and read with attention
                    your dispatch No. 537, of the 31st ultimo, in which you report the
                    insurrectionary movement undertaken by certain Haytian exiles at Miragoâne, and
                    transmit the correspondence exchanged between yourself and Mr. Damier in
                    relation thereto.</p>
                <p>It is observed that Mr. Damier states that the vessel which carried the
                    insurrectionary party to Hayti sailed under the flag of the United States. It is
                    desirable that the name and home port of the vessel be ascertained, in order
                    that it may be known whether she was in fact of American registry.</p>
                <p>I am &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
